welcome to another edition of technology  tuesday and today i mentioned a question  from  troy one of my youtube viewers love you  guys who's asking about  evernote so troy's question was nice  video a couple of questions  does the photo taken from the phone take  up more space than the scanned pdf  do you ever take photos of eight and a  half by eleven invoices receipts and so  on  or are those better scanned this is a  great question and when you're using  evernote you can either get a scan snap  or a scanner that can connect to  evernote or you can take pictures with  your phone  and i used to do everything scanning and  now i use  the phone mostly for convenience so in  terms of the sizing to answer your  question  i found that by keeping approximately  the same setting so they get the same  quality of image if you take a picture  with your phone it's gonna be five  times bigger than if you scan it through  a scan stamp which is what i use as my  scanner  so it does take up a lot more space  about five times bigger the second thing  to think about is if you use a scanner  with my scan snap it will straighten the  paper as it goes through so if you have  any creases or folds or bends in your  receipt  and maybe you've folded in your wallet  or you know your agreement was  crippled at the side the scanner will  flatten it out as it goes through the  scanning process  where with a phone you have to stomp it  out and make it flat  yourself so if you have a lot of folded  papers you want to use the scanner  and the other thing i found that when  you scan documents in  it's easier to take it back to stores so  if you are going to  return something right you bought  something at ikea you want to take it  back  they're much more willing to accept a  scanned version then a picture of a  receipt for whatever reason  and i guess one last thing when you're  taking a picture with your phone you  have to make sure that it's  focused so some of the early ones that i  took i would just take a picture  and then throw away the receipt and then  realize that when i looked at it on my  computer it was out of focus  and it couldn't pick up the text  recognition so it made it a lot harder  so there's a lot of reasons why to use  the scan snap scan instead of taking a  phone  having said that i still do everything  on the phone  and the main reason is convenience it's  just a lot faster  than putting things through the scanner  so i'll i'll lay out all the receipts on  the floor  or on the table or whatever it is and  just go snap snap snap snap snap snap  snap snap  and save it and they're all there so yes  you have to make sure they're flat  yes you have to make sure you know the  camera is in focus  yes it's going to be bigger on your  computer than uh  than scanning it in but i find that it  saves you some time so hopefully that  helps great question  for those of you watching you like the  video you can subscribe to the channel  uh you can support me by clicking on the  link in the description and  leave a comment you have a question  whatever note you have a comment about  this video leave it below  and love seeing those comments so thank  you and i'll see you soon
 

